ndary_3"}, {"content": "Understands key information in written texts about the communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands simple information in slow conversations about the communicative topics and vocabulary related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands key information in written texts about the communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands key information in written texts about the communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands simple information in slow conversations about the communicative topics and vocabulary related to this level.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "kind ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "saying or doing things to help people", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You are such a kind neighbor.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn2le04ob05aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about neighborhoods.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "friendly ", "type": "name"}, {"content": " kind; nice", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You are very friendly.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn2le04ob05aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "polite ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "thinking of other people's feelings", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You are too polite!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn2le04ob05aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "helpful ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "providing help", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You're very helpful.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn2le04ob05aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "neighbor", "type": "name"}, {"content": "someone who lives next to you", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I borrow sugar from my neighbour.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn2le04ob05aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "next door ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "in the house next to yours", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Angie lives next door.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn2le04ob05aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to bake  ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to cook something in the oven", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm baking a pie.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn2le04ob05aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Simple Connectors ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use connectors to join words and phrases.  They are usually found in the middle of a sentence. They connect ideas or sentences together.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":\"05\",\"columns\":\"03\",\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Connector </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Explanation </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Example </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"and \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Connects statements or ideas that are similar\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">You're kind <span class=\\\"strong\\\"> and</span> helpful.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"but\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Connects statements that express opposite ideas\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">That's very kind of you to ask <span class=\\\"strong\\\"> but</span> it's okay.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"or\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Gives options or choices\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">They are not nice <span class=\\\"strong\\\"> or</span> friendly.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"because\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Gives a reason \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">She is friendly <span class=\\\"strong\\\"> because</span> she helps us. </span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Asking to Borrow Things", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the modals <span class=\"strong\">can</span> or <span class=\"strong\">could</span> when you ask to borrow things.  <br/>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": " Structure of question:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Can/Could + Subject + borrow + object ? </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":\"03\",\"columns\":\"02\",\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Modals </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Examples </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"can\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Can I borrow a cup of sugar, please?</span>  \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"could\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Could we borrow your book, please? </span> <br/><span class=\\\"italic\\\">Could you lend* me your book tonight?</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">*</span>You use <span class=\"italic\">lend</span> to say that you give something to another person. You use <span class=\"italic\">borrow</span> to say that you get something from another person.", "type": "text"}]}, {"content": "engenn2le04ob05re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Choose 4 people you know.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Think of a word to describe each of them.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Give a reason about why you choose the word. Use the connector <span class=\"italic\">because</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Fill in the chart.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Person's Name\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Adjective\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Reason\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Molly</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">funny</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Molly is funny because she makes me laugh.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"&nbsp;\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"&nbsp;\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\